//! NVIDIA CUDA backend via [`cudarc`] (dynamic-loaded cuBLAS + cuSPARSE) plus
//! an optional raw cuFFT adapter for regular Complex32/Complex64 batches.
//!
//! This is the mature path. cudarc 0.19 ships safe wrappers for context,
//! stream, and buffer management, but the cuBLAS BLAS-1 surface and the
//! whole of cuSPARSE only exist as autogenerated FFI in the `sys`
//! submodules — no safe layer covers `axpy`, `dot`, `nrm2`, `scal`, or
//! the modern generic SpMV. So we drive those directly through
//! `cudarc::{cublas,cusparse,cusolver}::sys` wrappers:
//!
//! - BLAS-1 covers `f32`, `f64`, `Complex32`, `Complex64`. Complex routes
//!   through `cublasC*` / `cublasZ*`, using `dotc` (the conjugating dot)
//!   to satisfy the trait's Hermitian inner-product contract.
//! - `spmv_csr` uses the modern generic `cusparseSpMV` with descriptors
//!   created from caller-owned device buffers.
//! - Homogeneous dense `gemv_batched` / `gemm_batched` batches route through
//!   cuBLAS pointer-array batched calls, keeping block/frontal update
//!   workloads out of one-launch-per-tiny-op mode.
//! - Stable device-resident Krylov segments can be captured once as a CUDA
//!   graph and replayed to avoid rebuilding the same cuBLAS / cuSPARSE launch
//!   sequence on every iteration.
//! - `copy_d2d` is a real `cuMemcpyDtoDAsync_v2` via cudarc's safe
//!   `memcpy_dtod`, not host-staged.
//!
//! # Threading
//!
//! `CudaBackend::new` retains the primary context on the chosen device
//! and binds it to the calling thread, then creates one default stream,
//! one cuBLAS handle, and one cuSPARSE handle (both bound to that
//! stream). Multi-threaded use must `bind_to_thread()` per worker before
//! issuing ops.
//!
//! # Memory layout
//!
//! Device buffers are stored as `CudaSlice<u8>` so that storage works
//! uniformly for `f32` / `f64` / `Complex32` / `Complex64` / `i32` without
//! requiring a `DeviceRepr` impl on `num_complex::Complex` (orphan rule).
//! `len` is element count, not bytes; FFI calls cast the byte device
//! pointer to the typed pointer cuBLAS / cuSPARSE expect. The host-slice
//! `&[T]` ↔ `&[u8]` casts in `copy_h2d` / `copy_d2h` are sound because
//! `BufferElement` is `Copy + 'static + Send + Sync` and our supported
//! scalar types (`f32`, `f64`, `i32`, `Complex<f32>`, `Complex<f64>`)
//! are all `#[repr(C)]` POD with no padding.

